the glaucus's cerata Strike deals an additional [[/r 1d6[poison]]] damage. The glaucus can use this ability multiple times to increase the amount of poison damage dealt, to a maximum of 4d6 poison damage.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>@Compendium[battlezoo-bestiary-pf2e.pf2e-battlezoo-bestiary-effects.IeiDnzp25bTCfRl4]{Effect: Consume Poison (1 Dose)}</p>\n<p>@Compendium[battlezoo-bestiary-pf2e.pf2e-battlezoo-bestiary-effects.IDuxl9Id5fLl3Idk]{Effect: Consume Poison (2 Doses)}</p>\n<p>@Compendium[battlezoo-bestiary-pf2e.pf2e-battlezoo-bestiary-effects.EhdvyFEJ0pp2H8uY]{Effect: Consume Poison (3 Doses)}</p>\n<p>@Compendium[battlezoo-bestiary-pf2e.pf2e-battlezoo-bestiary-effects.IQY1fufWm1LTVwd8]{Effect: Consume Poison (4 Doses)}</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"free"},"category":"offensive","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"ownership":{"default":0,"ldigRFmLUDwvP1vo":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}}],"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{"pf2e":{"lootable":false},"core":{}},"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":80,"temp":0,"max":80,"details":""},"ac":{"value":18,"details":"","base":18},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":0,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"swim","label":"Swim","value":25}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"mental"},{"type":"precision"}],"resistances":[{"type":"poison","value":10}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":[],"details":""},"level":{"value":4},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Sailors' tales are full of fantastical creatures and monstrous beasts. While some who spend all their days on land might think these stories are exaggeration or imagination, those who have sailed the seas know there is more truth to them than not. From giant squid to jellyfish, strange creatures inhabit the depths of the world's oceans. Every ship that sails the sea is bound to encounter such a creature sooner or later. One of the lesser-known of these ocean dwellers is the giant glaucus slug, a monstrously oversized version of the common blue glaucus sea slug.</p>\n<p>Like their miniature kin, these shell-less mollusks float upside down on the water's surface using their long, slender appendages (cerata) to create surface tension. They do not locomote on their own but instead rely on winds and ocean currents to drift across the sea. A glaucus slug's blue and silver coloration acts as camouflage, blending into the deep blue of ocean water from above and the white reflected sunlight from the ocean's surface from below. While the silhouette of a glaucus slug resembles the outstretched wings of a dragon, these aquatic animals bear no relation to true dragons, despite their colorful alternative name, \"blue dragon slugs.\"</p>\n<p>By themselves, glaucus slugs are not especially dangerous. However, swimmers and sailors should still be wary when a glaucus slug appears. They both serve as a warning that venomous jellyfish may be nearby and can be deadly to encounter themselves when full of fresh jellyfish venom. The paralytic venom can leave the unfortunate victim vulnerable in the water to other animals' attacks.</p>\n<h2>Jellyfish Eaters</h2>\n<p>Glaucus slugs are one of the few animals capable of eating highly toxic jellyfishes. Perhaps even more terrifyingly, the glaucus can store—and even concentrate—consumed venom to use against future prey.</p>\n<h2>Monster Part Subsystem</h2>\n<p><strong>Giant Glaucus Slug Creature 4 </strong></p>\n<p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 12/27/50 gp</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning, piercing), armor (light), skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Stealth)</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, constitution, dexterity, energy resistant (positive), fortification, poison, sensory (low-light vision), strength, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary","authors":"Ryan King","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"creatureType":""},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":4},"dex":{"mod":5},"con":{"mod":4},"int":{"mod":-5},"wis":{"mod":1},"cha":{"mod":-5}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":9,"senses":[{"type":"low-light-vision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":14,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":13,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":7,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":13},"athletics":{"base":10},"stealth":{"base":11}},"traits":{"value":["animal","aquatic","mindless"],"rarity":"common","size":{"value":"sm"}},"customModifiers":{}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"prototypeToken":{"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"displayName":20,"displayBars":20,"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":true}},"height":1,"width":1,"disposition":-1,"name":"Giant Glaucus Slug","actorLink":false,"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"bar2":{"attribute":null},"randomImg":false,"light":{"alpha":0.25,"angle":360,"bright":0,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"speed":5,"intensity":5,"type":null,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1},"attenuation":0.5,"color":null,"negative":false,"priority":0},"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-pf2e/art/Tokens/giant_glaucus_slug.webp","scaleX":0.8,"scaleY":0.8,"tint":"#ffffff","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","alphaThreshold":0.75},"sight":{"angle":360,"enabled":false,"range":0,"brightness":1,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0